    "body": "@ankush-jain-akto - The fix works now. I was able to validate the fix successfully.\r\nThe only thing I observed in the docker logs for the dashboard was the below .... assume it can be ignored\r\n\r\n```\r\n[pool-2-thread-1] ERROR com.akto.utils.GithubSync - Err msg: Failed to download the zip archive from url https://github.com/akto-api-security/tests-library/archive/refs/heads/master.zip. Error PKIX path building failed: sun.security.provider.certpath.SunCertPathBuilderException: unable to find valid certification path to requested target\r\nClass: sun.security.ssl.Alert\r\nFile: Alert.java\r\nLine: 131\r\n[pool-2-thread-1] INFO com.akto.utils.TestTemplateUtils - Failed to load test templates from github, trying to load from local directory\r\n[pool-2-thread-1] INFO com.akto.listener.InitializerListener - Loading template files from directory\r\n[pool-2-thread-1] INFO com.akto.utils.TestTemplateUtils - Loaded test templates from local directory\r\nin Home::execute: settings IS_SAAS to false\r\n```\r\n\r\nScreenshot below of the working fix.\r\n**Let me know if you need anything else to check from my end before I close this issue.** \r\nThanks for your support.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"769\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/akto-api-security/akto/assets/94514187/55d982f0-d8a9-436e-8fe2-92a0771f7def\">\r\n",
